<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ruleset name="Groundwork Common Post Portal — PHP compatibility">

	<description>
		Does the source actually run on the PHP version the plugin header
		claims? That is a different question from "does it match the coding
		standard", it fails for different reasons, and it is cheaper to read on
		its own — so it stays a separate run with its own ruleset rather than
		another `rule ref` inside phpcs.xml.dist.

		The floor lives in the plugin header. It is repeated below as the
		default so a local `composer compat` needs no arguments; CI overrides it
		with `--runtime-set testVersion` from the header itself, because a floor
		typed in two places is a floor that will disagree with itself.
	</description>

	<!--
		Named, not found-by-scanning-and-excluded. This is the same list as
		phpcs.xml.dist's, kept for the same reason, and tests/LintTargetsTest.php
		fails if the two ever disagree — read the long comment there and in
		phpcs.xml.dist before editing either.

		The short version: scanning `.` and passing an ignore list matches
		ABSOLUTE paths, which makes an exclusion a claim about the machine's
		directory layout rather than about this repository. It has already
		failed in both directions for the lint run: first by scanning the stale
		plugin copies under `.claude/worktrees/`, then, once those were
		excluded, by matching the whole repository whenever the checkout itself
		sits under `.claude/worktrees/` and silently scanning nothing at all.

		This run carried exactly the first of those bugs until now. Its ignore
		list named vendor, node_modules and tests and nothing else, so from the
		repo root it checked every worktree copy of the plugin as well as the
		plugin, and `.dev/` besides.
	-->
	<file>groundwork-common-post-portal.php</file>
	<file>uninstall.php</file>
	<file>inc</file>
	<file>blocks</file>

	<arg name="extensions" value="php"/>
	<arg name="colors"/>
	<arg name="basepath" value="."/>
	<arg name="parallel" value="8"/>
	<arg value="ps"/>

	<rule ref="PHPCompatibilityWP"/>

	<config name="testVersion" value="7.4-"/>

</ruleset>
